course: dictionary
lesson: 2211
title: Words for places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A county is a part of a state or country. It has its own name, its own towns and its own local government, which means the people who look after things nearby. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and often give clues.
explain: Read this: «An address goes in this order: the name, then house number and street, then town or city, then state or county, then postcode or ZIP code.» The county comes after the town and before the postcode, so it is a bigger area that the town sits inside. Check it by swapping in your meaning: a part of a state or country still makes sense there.
explain: Read this: «At the county gala he wins by a fingertip.» A gala is a special swimming event, and county tells you it is for swimmers from a whole area, not just one pool or one school. The word county can also appear in everyday life, like «the county library», which is a library that serves a whole county.
fact: A county is a part of a state or country with its own name, towns and local government.
fact: Most US states are divided into counties, and England, Wales and Ireland are divided into counties too.
fact: «County» can also describe a team or event for a whole area, like «the county under-11s».
fact: Context clues, such as the words in an address, can help you work out what a word means.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «An address goes in this order: the name, then house number and street, then town or city, then state or county, then postcode or ZIP code.» In an address, what does county mean? | A small house on a farm | A fair with rides and food | *A part of a state or country with its own name and local government | A type of postcode
exercise: «At the county gala he wins by a fingertip.» What does county gala suggest? | A swimming race only for toddlers | A quiet day at the seaside | A school lesson in the pool | *A swimming event for swimmers from the whole area
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Ruby... discovered grandma had the best poker face in the county.» that names a part of a country. | countryside | grandma | cards | *county
test: «Otters have been reported again in every county of England.» What does every county of England mean? | Every county in Scotland | Every river in England | Every town in England | *Every one of the parts England is split into
test: «Connor and Tyler both get picked for the county under-11s.» What does county under-11s tell you? | A team only for players from one school | *A team for young players from the whole area | A group of cows from a farm | Fast runners in the same class
exam: Which is the best meaning of county? | A kind of fair with games and food | A very big city | *A part of a state or country with its own name, towns and local government | The capital city of a country
